  "items": [
    {
      "name": "What is a patulous Eustachian tube",
      "char_file": "체중계_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Could a diuretic or",
        "birth control pill be behind",
        "that strange echo in your ear",
        "",
        "It happens when the Eustachian",
        "tube stays open instead of",
        "closing the way it normally does"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rapid weight loss",
      "char_file": "체중계_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Weight loss is the risk factor",
        "doctors mention most often",
        "",
        "A fat pad around the tube",
        "thins out, so it loses",
        "the support that keeps it closed",
        "",
        "About one in five patients",
        "after bariatric surgery",
        "report symptoms like this"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Certain medications",
      "char_file": "이뇨제_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A less talked about cause:",
        "certain medications",
        "",
        "Diuretics and estrogen-based",
        "birth control pills",
        "have both been linked to it",
        "",
        "If symptoms started around",
        "a new prescription,",
        "mention that timing to your doctor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Stress and exercise make it worse",
      "char_file": "이뇨제_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Stress and exercise",
        "tend to make symptoms worse",
        "",
        "Ask your doctor whether",
        "an alternative medication",
        "makes sense for you"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Relief when lying down, worse standing",
      "char_file": "이불_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Lying down or bending forward",
        "often brings quick relief",
        "",
        "Blood flow shifts toward your head",
        "and swells tissue around the tube,",
        "narrowing it again"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Saline spray and seeing a doctor",
      "char_file": "비강스프레이_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Try saline nasal spray",
        "with your head tilted down",
        "for quick relief",
        "",
        "If symptoms stick around",
        "or affect your daily life,",
        "book a visit with",
        "an ENT doctor"
      ]
    }
  ],
